    "caveats": [
      "All monetary fields are stored as direct currency amounts (not cents). Currency is not explicitly labeled for orders and line items; part retail price is USD, while supply cost is labeled only as currency.",
      "Use orders.o_totalprice for order-level revenue. Do not sum it after joining orders to lineitem, because each order is repeated once per line item and order revenue will be overstated.",
      "Line-item revenue concepts differ: l_extendedprice is pre-discount/pre-tax; net revenue is l_extendedprice * (1 - l_discount); tax-inclusive revenue additionally multiplies by (1 + l_tax). Discounts and taxes are fractions from 0 to 1, not percentages.",
      "A line item's supplier and part are independently joinable to supplier and part. To associate a line item to a specific part-supplier offering in partsupp, join on both (l_partkey = ps_partkey AND l_suppkey = ps_suppkey); joining on only one key causes fan-out.",
      "partsupp is one row per part\u2013supplier pair. Joining part or supplier to partsupp multiplies those entities, so aggregate entity-level measures such as supplier account balance or part retail price before that join.",
      "Customer and supplier account balances can be negative; they are balances, not sales or profit.",
      "Order dates range from 1992-01-01 to 1998-08-02, while line shipping, commitment, and receipt dates extend through 1998-12-25. Select the date appropriate to the business event.",
      "o_shippriority has only observed value 0, so it cannot meaningfully segment results by shipping priority.",
      "Order keys range to 60000 but only 15000 orders are present; keys should not be interpreted as a contiguous row count."
    ],
